== Abstract ==

This proposal adds OP_TEMPLATEHASH, OP_CHECKSIGFROMSTACK, and OP_INTERNALKEY to Bitcoin Tapscript while retaining Reduced Data Temporary Softfork (RDTS) restrictions. It adapts the operation set proposed in BIP 448 to a validation context that rejects unknown OP_SUCCESS operations at consensus.

TEMPLATEHASH and INTERNALKEY follow BIPs 446 and 349. CHECKSIGFROMSTACK narrows BIP 348 to signatures over the current input's template hash. This document specifies that restriction and its interaction with RDTS and existing signature rules. The implementation is running on an experimental signet. A production activation mechanism is not specified.

This is an independently published, unnumbered BIP draft. No number has been assigned by the BIP editors; the BIP and Assigned header fields remain "?". It is not a replacement for BIP 448.

